The following code snippet contains a bug:

```php
    public function toBase()
    {
        return $this->query->getQuery();
    }
```

The code fails the following tests:

Test `Illuminate\Tests\Database\DatabaseEloquentSoftDeletesIntegrationTest::testSoftDeletesAreNotRetrievedFromRelationshipBaseQuery`:
            
```php
    public function testSoftDeletesAreNotRetrievedFromRelationshipBaseQuery()
    {
        [, $abigail] = $this->createUsers();

        $abigail->posts()->create(['title' => 'Foo']);
        $abigail->posts()->create(['title' => 'Bar'])->delete();

        $query = $abigail->posts()->toBase();

        $this->assertInstanceOf(Builder::class, $query);
        $this->assertCount(1, $query->get());
    }
```

The error message is:

```
Failed asserting that actual size 2 matches expected size 1.
```

Please provide a fixed version of the buggy function, and only that function without additional imports. Make sure the code is between ``` and ```.
```php
    public function toBase()
    {
        return $this->query->getQuery()->whereNull($this->getModel()->getTable(). '.deleted_at');
    }
```
